[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `argc != 2` is checked *before* any parsing | `driver 42 42` prints usage; the valid seed is never looked at | `argc_extra_args_are_not_parsed_even_if_first_is_valid` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | Usage message interpolates `argv[0]` with `%s` | Whatever `argv[0]` holds is echoed verbatim, including `%s%d%n`, tabs, newlines and invalid UTF-8 | `usage_message_echoes_argv0_verbatim` |
