[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   positive) and is why no test asserts a negative `%d`. It is not a fidelity
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   risk in any case: Rust's `{}` and C's `%d` agree on every `i32`, including
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `i32::MIN`.
